# Discord Bot Development Patterns

## Objective
Establish consistent patterns for Discord.js v14 bot development, focusing on reliability, user experience, and maintainability.

## Context
- discord.js v14.18.0
- Slash commands and interactions
- Button-based pagination
- Scheduled notifications
- Economic calendar data display

## Core Patterns

### Command Structure

#### Slash Command Definition
Every command must follow this structure:

✅ **Good**:
```typescript
import { ChatInputCommandInteraction, SlashCommandBuilder } from 'discord.js';

export const commandName = {
  data: new SlashCommandBuilder()
    .setName('calendar')
    .setDescription('Shows upcoming economic calendar events'),

  async execute(interaction: ChatInputCommandInteraction) {
    // Implementation
  },
};
```

#### Command Registration
Commands are deployed via `deploy-commands.ts`:
- Reads all command files from `src/commands/`
- Registers with Discord API
- Runs before bot starts

### Interaction Handling

#### Universal Interaction Pattern
ALWAYS handle all possible interaction states:

✅ **Good**:
```typescript
async execute(interaction: ChatInputCommandInteraction) {
  try {
    // Defer early if operation might take time
    if (!interaction.deferred && !interaction.replied) {
      await interaction.deferReply();
    }

    // ... perform operation ...

    // Respond based on current state
    if (interaction.deferred || interaction.replied) {
      await interaction.editReply(content);
    } else {
      await interaction.reply(content);
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error in command:', error);

    // Safe error response
    if (interaction.isRepliable()) {
      const errorMsg = { content: 'An error occurred', ephemeral: true };

      if (interaction.deferred || interaction.replied) {
        await interaction.editReply(errorMsg);
      } else {
        await interaction.reply(errorMsg);
      }
    }
  }
}
```

❌ **Avoid**:
```typescript
// Missing defer for long operations
async execute(interaction: ChatInputCommandInteraction) {
  const data = await longOperation(); // May timeout
  await interaction.reply(data); // Fails if > 3 seconds
}

// Not checking interaction state
await interaction.reply(content); // May fail if already deferred
```

### Button Interactions

#### Pagination Pattern
✅ **Good**:
```typescript
if (interaction.isButton()) {
  const { customId } = interaction;

  // Validate button is for this feature
  if (!['calendar_prev', 'calendar_next'].includes(customId)) return;

  // Retrieve cached state
  const messageId = interaction.message.id;
  const cache = globalThis.calendarCache?.get(messageId);

  if (!cache) {
    await interaction.reply({ content: 'No pagination data found.', ephemeral: true });
    return;
  }

  let { pages, currentPage } = cache;

  // Update page based on button
  if (customId === 'calendar_prev' && currentPage > 0) currentPage--;
  else if (customId === 'calendar_next' && currentPage < pages.length - 1) currentPage++;

  // Build new embed and buttons
  const embed = buildEmbed(pages[currentPage], currentPage, pages.length);
  const row = new ActionRowBuilder<ButtonBuilder>().addComponents(
    new ButtonBuilder()
      .setCustomId('calendar_prev')
      .setLabel('Previous page')
      .setStyle(ButtonStyle.Secondary)
      .setDisabled(currentPage === 0),
    new ButtonBuilder()
      .setCustomId('calendar_next')
      .setLabel('Next page')
      .setStyle(ButtonStyle.Secondary)
      .setDisabled(currentPage === pages.length - 1),
  );

  // Update cache and message
  globalThis.calendarCache.set(messageId, { pages, currentPage });
  await interaction.update({ embeds: [embed], components: [row] });
}
```

### Embed Construction

#### Consistent Embed Formatting
✅ **Good**:
```typescript
export function buildCalendarEmbed(
  pageBlocks: string[],
  pageIndex: number,
  totalPages: number
): EmbedBuilder {
  const embed = new EmbedBuilder()
    .setTitle('Economic Calendar')
    .setFooter({ text: `Page ${pageIndex + 1} of ${totalPages}` })
    .setColor(0x7289da);

  for (const block of pageBlocks) {
    const lines = block.split('\n');
    const headingLine = lines[0] || 'No Date';
    const rest = lines.slice(1).join('\n');

    embed.addFields({
      name: headingLine,
      value: rest || '\u200B' // Zero-width space for empty fields
    });
  }

  return embed;
}
```

#### Notification Embeds
- Use appropriate colors for context (warning, info, success)
- Include timestamp information
- Format data clearly for mobile viewing
- Show performance indicators when available

### Global State Management

#### Persistent State Pattern
✅ **Good**:
```typescript
// Declare global types
declare global {
  var calendarCache: Map<string, { pages: string[][]; currentPage: number }>;
  var notificationTimeouts: Map<string, NodeJS.Timeout[]>;
}

// Initialize with fallback
globalThis.calendarCache = globalThis.calendarCache || new Map();
globalThis.notificationTimeouts = globalThis.notificationTimeouts || new Map();

// Clean up when needed
function clearOldCache(): void {
  // Implement cleanup logic
  globalThis.calendarCache.clear();
}
```

### Error Handling Best Practices

#### Graceful Degradation
✅ **Good**:
```typescript
try {
  const events = await scrapeEconomicCalendar();

  if (events.length === 0) {
    // Graceful handling of empty results
    const msg = 'No calendar events found.';
    if (interaction.deferred || interaction.replied) {
      await interaction.editReply(msg);
    } else {
      await interaction.reply(msg);
    }
    return;
  }

  // Continue with normal flow
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Error scraping calendar:', error);

  // User-friendly error message
  const errorMsg = 'An error occurred while fetching calendar events.';
  if (interaction.deferred || interaction.replied) {
    await interaction.editReply(errorMsg);
  } else {
    await interaction.reply({ content: errorMsg, ephemeral: true });
  }
}
```

### Channel Communication

#### Sending Messages
✅ **Good**:
```typescript
export async function sendEmbed(embed: EmbedBuilder): Promise<Message | null> {
  try {
    const channel = await discordClient.channels.fetch(CHANNEL_ID) as TextChannel;

    if (!channel || !channel.isTextBased()) {
      console.error('Channel not found or not text-based');
      return null;
    }

    return await channel.send({ embeds: [embed] });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error sending notification embed:', error);
    return null;
  }
}
```

#### Editing Messages
✅ **Good**:
```typescript
async function updateNotification(msg: Message | null, newEmbed: EmbedBuilder): Promise<void> {
  if (msg && typeof msg.edit === 'function') {
    try {
      await msg.edit({ embeds: [newEmbed] });
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error editing message:', error);
    }
  }
}
```

### Scheduling and Timers

#### Notification Scheduling Pattern
✅ **Good**:
```typescript
export async function scheduleNotifications(): Promise<void> {
  // Clear existing schedules first
  clearScheduledNotifications();

  const events = await getStoredEvents();
  if (events.length === 0) return;

  const groups = groupEvents(events);

  for (const [groupKey, groupEvents] of groups.entries()) {
    const eventTime = parseEventDateTime(groupEvents[0]);
    if (!eventTime) continue;

    const notifTime = addMinutes(eventTime, -30);
    const delay = differenceInMilliseconds(notifTime, new Date());

    if (delay > 0) {
      const timeoutId = setTimeout(async () => {
        const embed = buildNotificationEmbed(30, groupEvents);
        await sendEmbed(embed);
      }, delay);

      // Store timeout for cleanup
      const timeouts = globalThis.notificationTimeouts.get(groupKey) || [];
      timeouts.push(timeoutId);
      globalThis.notificationTimeouts.set(groupKey, timeouts);

      console.log(`Scheduled notification in ${(delay / 1000).toFixed(1)}s`);
    }
  }
}

function clearScheduledNotifications(): void {
  globalThis.notificationTimeouts.forEach(timeouts => {
    timeouts.forEach(id => clearTimeout(id));
  });
  globalThis.notificationTimeouts.clear();
}
```

### Bot Initialization

#### Proper Startup Sequence
✅ **Good**:
```typescript
export async function initializeDiscordBot(): Promise<void> {
  // Register event handlers
  discordClient.on('interactionCreate', async (interaction: Interaction) => {
    try {
      if (interaction.isChatInputCommand()) {
        // Handle commands
      }
      if (interaction.isButton()) {
        // Handle buttons
      }
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error in interactionCreate:', error);
      if (interaction.isRepliable()) {
        await interaction.reply({ content: 'Something went wrong.', ephemeral: true });
      }
    }
  });

  // Return promise that resolves when ready
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    discordClient.once('ready', () => {
      console.log(`Discord bot logged in as ${discordClient.user?.tag}`);
      resolve();
    });

    discordClient.login(DISCORD_TOKEN).catch(reject);
  });
}
```

## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

❌ **Don't**:
1. Forget to defer long operations (>3s)
2. Reply to already-replied interactions
3. Forget to disable buttons at boundaries
4. Use bare `any` types for Discord types
5. Forget to clean up timeouts/intervals
6. Send non-ephemeral error messages
7. Forget to validate interaction state
8. Hard-code IDs or tokens in source

✅ **Do**:
1. Always defer if operation might take time
2. Check interaction state before replying
3. Disable pagination buttons appropriately
4. Use proper Discord.js types
5. Clean up scheduled tasks
6. Use ephemeral for error/debug messages
7. Validate all user input
8. Use environment variables for config

## Testing Considerations
- Test with FAKE_DATE environment variable for date-dependent features
- Verify pagination works with different data sizes
- Test error scenarios (network failures, invalid data)
- Verify notification timing accuracy
- Test interaction timeout handling
